    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming two-bedroom bungalow on circa 0.35 acre site with the beautiful Oweniny River forming the picturesque background, and less than 1km from Bangor Erris village providing all amenities.\r\n\r\nNestled in the peaceful and picturesque townland of Ballynumera, just outside Bangor Erris, this charming two-bedroom bungalow enjoys a picturesque setting on approximately 0.35 acre. With the meandering Oweniny River visible to the rear, the property offers a wonderful sense of peace, privacy and connection with the surrounding countryside. Quietly positioned yet remarkably convenient, this is a home that combines rural tranquility with easy access to the amenities and attractions of North Mayo.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, two bedrooms, kitchen/dining room, sitting room, utility room and shower room. \r\n\r\nBangor village is less than a kilometre away and provides a welcoming community atmosphere together with a range of everyday amenities, including a national school, church, community playground, grocery shop, pharmacy, post office, restaurants and bars. Kiltane GAA Club is approximately 400 metres from the property, while the renowned Bangor Trail begins close by, making it easy to step straight into the spectacular landscapes for which this part of Mayo is famous.\r\n\r\nFor those who enjoy the outdoors, the surrounding area is an exceptional playground. Carrowmore Lake is approximately five minutes away by car, while a selection of beautiful, unspoilt beaches can be reached in under twenty minutes. The property is also ideally positioned for exploring Wild Nephin National Park and the wider Wild Atlantic Way, with attractions including Blacksod Bay, Broadhaven Bay, the Céide Fields, Carrowteigue, Carne Golf Course and the North Mayo Sculpture Trail all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nDespite its tranquil countryside setting, the property is within convenient commuting distance of Belmullet, Ballina, Crossmolina, Castlebar and Westport.\r\n\r\nBallynumera offers an opportunity to embrace a slower pace of life without sacrificing convenience. Here, the winding Oweniny River, expansive countryside, nearby mountains, lakes and Atlantic coastline combine with the warmth and community spirit of Bangor Erris to create a truly appealing place to call home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway \r\n1.61m (5'3\") x 4.31m (14'2\")\r\nBright hall with a tiled floor, central pendant light, and a large window providing ample natural light.\r\n\r\nSitting Room \r\n4.78m (15'8\") x 3.79m (12'5\")\r\nSpacious room with a carpet floor, central pendant light, open fireplace and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nKitchen \r\n4.3m (14'1\") x 2.64m (8'8\")\r\nFitted kitchen with tiled floor, tiled splashback, integrated oven/hob, fridge/freezer and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nUtility Room \r\n1.87m (6'2\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\r\nPractical space with a tiled floor, and two windows flooding the space with natural light.\r\n\r\nShower Room \r\n3.05m (10'0\") x 2.02m (6'8\")\r\nFully tiled with a toilet, wash hand basin with vanity unit, and electric shower. A window provides natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\n4.36m (14'4\") x 3.3m (10'10\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, built-in wardrobes and two windows providing natural light and countryside views.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\n4.45m (14'7\") x 2.72m (8'11\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, built-in wardrobes and a window providing natural light and countryside views."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming two-bedroom bungalow on circa 0.35 acre site\r\nPicturesque rural setting with views towards the winding Oweniny River\r\nOil-fired central heating \r\nOpen fireplace providing warmth & charm\r\nBangor Village less than 1km away, with school, shop, pharmacy, post office, restaurants, bars, & other amenities\r\nKiltane GAA Club approximately 400m away\r\nThe start of Bangor Trail in close proximity\r\nCarrowmore Lake approximately 5 minutes away with beautiful beaches less than a 20 minute drive away\r\nIdeal base for exploring North Mayo & The Wild Atlantic Way, including Wild Nephin National Park, Blacksod Bay, Broadhaven Bay, & The Céide Fields.\r\nWithin commuting distance of Belmullet, Ballina, Crossmolina, Castlebar, & Westport"
      },
